1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:24,880
What the hell is this?

2
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:33,120
A worn-down castle from the restoration period. Must have been abandoned or forgotten because the location is inconvenient. Or so I assume.

3
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:39,160
What a sick joke. Those demon bastards are living it up like lords in that thing.

4
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:45,160
And you're certain that someone from the village was taken here, there is no doubt?

5
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:51,360
Yes. You have my word. We trapped her up to the castle's tower, but found nothing.

6
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:57,180
She couldn't have vanished into thin air, idiot. How could you let them ditch you?

7
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:58,320
I'm truly sorry.

8
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:03,420
So, this means another woman has disappeared in 24 hours.

9
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,600
Despite the Demon Slayer Corps being on the alert, they still got us.

10
00:01:08,040 --> 00:01:10,460
No one's expecting anything from you chumps.

11
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:16,340
Hmm. Lucky for us. We may not have gotten here too late after all.

12
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:17,640
Bastard!

13
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:17,700
Bastard!

14
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:39,980
I had a feeling that I should have disposed of them last night.

15
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:45,120
Yes.

16
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,820
I'm sorry.

17
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,760
Bye!

18
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:02,800
Bye!

19
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:08,560
Bye!

20
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:09,340
Bye!

21
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:39,220
Take that!

22
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:48,220
You two head back to the village.

23
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:51,720
From here on, just the wind Hashira and I will proceed.

24
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:53,020
But, sir...

25
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:54,840
The two of you will be a hindrance.

26
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,580
Now get out of my sight.

27
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:03,940
Shinazugawa, something isn't right about this place.

28
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:06,740
No kidding. I don't like this either.

29
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:10,740
I've never seen so many demons swarming around like this.

30
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:20,740
Wind breathing, second form!

31
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:28,740
Walls, purifying wind!

32
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:36,740
Serpent breathing, fifth form.

33
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:46,740
Slithering serpent!

34
00:03:46,740 --> 00:03:48,740
That was close, huh?

35
00:03:48,740 --> 00:03:50,740
I didn't ask for your help!

36
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:54,740
So powerful!

37
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:56,740
They're not just any demon slaters.

38
00:03:56,740 --> 00:03:58,740
I may hush you up!

39
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:00,740
Hey, bastard!

40
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:02,740
I'm taking her back!

41
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:04,740
Along with your rotten head!

42
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:06,740
Step aside!

43
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:10,740
There's no one in sight to these scum!

44
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:11,740
Just what are you?

45
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:12,740
Come, Roses!

46
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:15,740
Enough!

47
00:04:15,740 --> 00:04:16,740
There's more!

48
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:21,740
Where the hell are all these things coming from anyway?

49
00:04:21,740 --> 00:04:22,740
Focus on saving the woman.

50
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:23,740
Leave this to me.

51
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:24,740
Leave this to me.

52
00:04:24,740 --> 00:04:25,740
I can handle them on my own.

53
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:26,740
I was getting bored anyway.

54
00:04:26,740 --> 00:04:27,740
Leave the rest to you!

55
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:32,740
Serpent breathing, third form.

56
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:33,740
Third form!

57
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:38,740
Serpent breathing, third form!

58
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:40,740
There's more!

59
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:41,740
Where the hell are all these things coming from anyway?

60
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:45,740
Where the hell are all these things coming from anyway?

61
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:46,740
Focus on saving the woman.

62
00:04:46,740 --> 00:04:47,740
Leave this to me.

63
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:49,740
I can handle them on my own.

64
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:54,740
Serpent Breathing, 3rd Form

65
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:02,740
Coil Choke

66
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:14,740
You know, even with your friends, you're still not gonna win

67
00:05:14,740 --> 00:05:16,740
Save us some time and die

68
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:32,740
Wind Breathing, 4th Form

69
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:38,740
Rising Dust Storm

70
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:41,740
Really now

71
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:43,740
If you wanna back that badly

72
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:45,740
Stop it! What are you doing?

73
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:47,740
Then take her!

74
00:05:49,740 --> 00:06:03,740
What is this?

75
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:05,740
What is this?

76
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:19,740
Get back here, you bastard!

77
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:21,740
What the hell is going on?

78
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:35,740
Hey Shinazugawa, what was that just now?

79
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:49,740
And where did those demons vanish to?

80
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:51,740
Hell if I know

81
00:06:51,740 --> 00:07:05,740
You sure I can drop you off at the crossroads ahead?

82
00:07:05,740 --> 00:07:19,740
You sure I can drop you off at the crossroads ahead?

83
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:25,740
I...

84
00:07:25,740 --> 00:07:49,920
Miss Canal, thank you for all your hard work.

85
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:51,760
Welcome back.

86
00:07:55,740 --> 00:08:13,180
Master, I've returned from my mission.

87
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:19,860
The incident at the Swordsmith Village is as I described the other day.

88
00:08:19,860 --> 00:08:29,180
Mr. Tokito, Ms. Kanroji, also, Kamado and a few others were able to defeat two upper ranks in one night.

89
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:34,400
Not only that, but Ms. Nezuko appears to have conquered the sun.

90
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:39,420
Meaning, major developments are just on the horizon for us.

91
00:08:40,220 --> 00:08:40,860
Yes.

92
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:47,680
It's more than likely that Muzan Kibutsuji is planning to send his demons to abduct Ms. Nezuko.

93
00:08:49,740 --> 00:08:53,860
He wants nothing more than to take possession of the demon who's conquered the sun.

94
00:08:59,760 --> 00:09:01,060
I'll be leaving soon.

95
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:06,540
An emergency Hashira meeting has been issued by our master, so I'll be heading to the Ubuyashiki mansion.

96
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:10,400
While I'm gone, I have a favor to ask.

97
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,500
Can you take care of Ms. Nezuko?

98
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,320
I'm counting on you.

99
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:32,460
Oh, I see.

100
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,160
So they're moving already.

101
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:37,140
Then is everyone in the village all right?

102
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:42,500
I don't know enough to say for sure, but they're worried more demons might come at night,

103
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:44,900
so they've been working to get the place restored and moved.

104
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:46,760
That makes sense.

105
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:50,780
It's a miracle that it wasn't worse, seeing as two upper ranks showed up.

106
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:55,140
And they were both such unbelievable opponents.

107
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:06,380
The Demon Slayer Corps have a few so-called empty villages built for such occasions,

108
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:08,840
to move right away if anything happened.

109
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:09,960
Really?

110
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:14,580
It just goes to show you how farsighted the master and the others are.

111
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:19,660
Are you sure you should be gorging yourself like that after being unconscious for seven days?

112
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:20,640
Sure.

113
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:23,500
After all, Ms. Konroji always eats plenty.

114
00:10:24,380 --> 00:10:27,320
If you ask me, that one's actually something of an outlier.

115
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:35,440
It only took three days for Ms. Love and Mr. Mist to fully recover, right?

116
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:36,660
That's right.

117
00:10:36,780 --> 00:10:37,540
They're amazing.

118
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:41,360
So you're inching closer to the level, little by little.

119
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:45,620
Well, if it means you'll get well faster, I guess that's fine.

120
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:46,420
Yup.

121
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:48,680
It's a miracle everyone survived.

122
00:10:49,100 --> 00:10:49,520
Yes!

123
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:50,400
Ooh!

124
00:10:50,540 --> 00:10:52,440
I've been dying to ask you this.

125
00:10:53,020 --> 00:10:54,880
I heard something wild happen to your sister.

126
00:10:55,540 --> 00:10:56,400
Will she be okay?

127
00:10:57,180 --> 00:10:58,040
Uh, yes.

128
00:10:58,040 --> 00:11:02,440
She's been strolling around outside while the sun is out, hasn't she?

129
00:11:04,280 --> 00:11:05,700
Isn't that a big deal?

130
00:11:06,020 --> 00:11:07,820
Like a really big deal?

131
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:10,640
We're having someone look into it further.

132
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:14,720
But still, we're not sure if she's more human now.

133
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,540
We're just evolving as a demon.

134
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:19,780
Is it Lady Kojo who's looking into that?

135
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:20,560
Nope.

136
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:21,420
Ms. Tamayo.

137
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:23,300
Who is Ms. Tamayo?

138
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:27,920
I told you not to stuck your face like that.

139
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:28,820
You're still recovering.

140
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:30,420
Show some restraints.

141
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:33,140
What a close call.

142
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:37,020
Now that your sister's conquered the sun,

143
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:38,920
a lot's going to be happening around here.

144
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:42,100
All the Demon Slayers have been ordered to go on alert.

145
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:45,340
And I'm told the Hashira are having an emergency meeting.

146
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:48,160
Whatever's happening, it has me worried.

147
00:11:57,920 --> 00:12:06,460
Are we the last to show up?

148
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:08,400
I see we've kept you waiting.

149
00:12:08,860 --> 00:12:09,600
Forgive us.

150
00:12:11,060 --> 00:12:12,340
You needn't worry.

151
00:12:13,300 --> 00:12:14,720
Thank you for taking that mission.

152
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:16,900
No problem.

153
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:22,760
Konroji and Tokito, I heard you two battled some upper ranks.

154
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:24,020
Hmm.

155
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:25,300
It was intense.

156
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:27,800
At one point, I truly thought I was done for.

157
00:12:28,140 --> 00:12:29,740
But we all pulled through as a team.

158
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:31,320
Right, Muichiro?

159
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:38,440
I wish I could have been there too.

160
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:42,040
Man, how come I never get to run into any upper ranks?

161
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:44,660
It's out of our control.

162
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,020
All we can do is leave it to fate.

163
00:12:48,220 --> 00:12:51,980
Konroji and Tokito, physically, how have you been since?

164
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:54,680
Oh, I'm okay.

165
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,040
Thank you for asking.

166
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:58,680
Wow, he's really worried about me.

167
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,080
So am I.

168
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:02,560
Although I haven't fully recovered yet.

169
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:04,540
Good to hear.

170
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:07,840
Losing any more Hashira would put the core at risk.

171
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:11,980
Defeating two upper ranks without losing your lives was noble of you.

172
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:14,600
Something's different about you two.

173
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,980
And your wounds healed abnormally quickly.

174
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,000
What exactly happened?

175
00:13:20,140 --> 00:13:21,500
Concerning their changes.

176
00:13:21,980 --> 00:13:23,880
I trust the Master will explain everything.

177
00:13:29,520 --> 00:13:31,680
Thank you all for patiently waiting.

178
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:39,860
Today's Hashira meeting will be conducted by myself as a stand-in for Kaguya Ubuyashiki.

179
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:44,200
You see, his conditions worsened.

180
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:49,480
And therefore, Kaguya, the head of our family, can never appear before you again.

181
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,980
I'm sorry.

182
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:52,740
I know this must be hard.

183
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:53,240
Understood.

184
00:13:53,240 --> 00:14:12,940
I pray that the Master finds the strength.

185
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:16,120
The strength to let the light of his life continue burning,

186
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,620
even one day longer.

187
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:21,320
And I pray that you can stay strong yourself, Lady Amane.

188
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:28,740
From the bottom of my heart, I want to thank each and every one of you.

189
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:36,420
I believe that you're already aware of this, but now that a demon who's conquered sunlight has appeared,

190
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:41,880
it's a given that Musan Kibutsuji will make a frenzied attempt to come after her,

191
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:44,920
so that he, too, can conquer the sun.

192
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:48,880
An all-out war of immense scale is approaching us.

193
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:56,220
But there is hope that was given to us by Lady Kanroji and Lord Tokito.

194
00:14:57,760 --> 00:15:03,560
I'm told that a unique-looking mark appeared on the both of you during your previous battle.

195
00:15:04,140 --> 00:15:09,860
I ask of you, please teach us what you two did to manifest your marks in battle.

196
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:12,200
Our marks?

197
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:15,720
During the Sengoku period,

198
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:22,260
the swordsmen of first breathing who had driven Musan Kibutsuji to the brink of defeat.

199
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:27,640
What they all shared in common was the mark each of them bore,

200
00:15:28,100 --> 00:15:30,060
a mark similar to demonic patterns.

201
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:36,300
There are those who are aware of this, having heard through word of mouth.

202
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,980
It's the first time I'm hearing of it.

203
00:15:39,580 --> 00:15:41,300
Why has this been kept secret from us?

204
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:48,520
Many swordsmen sought to manifest a mark and brooded over not having one appear despite their efforts.

205
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:54,560
That is why, much of the lore surrounding this mark remained shrouded in mystery.

206
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:59,420
Perhaps because at the time, it was not seen as vital enough to preserve.

207
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:07,420
Or perhaps because there was no one to pass it on to, during the many times the Demon Slayer core faced annihilation.

208
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:13,280
There only remains a single record that describes the manifestation of these marks.

209
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:21,460
When one person bearing the mark appears, those around him also manifest marks as if resonating with him.

210
00:16:21,460 --> 00:16:31,360
One of the first breathing swordsmen wrote this in his notes.

211
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:33,820
That's the only clue we have to work with.

212
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:39,820
However, the first person of our generation to have the mark has appeared.

213
00:16:39,820 --> 00:16:49,420
Shockingly, that person is not a Hashira, but Lord Tanjiro Kamado, the first person to bear the mark.

214
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:59,280
The only problem is that he himself seemed unable to describe exactly how his mark appeared, so we decided to revisit it another time.

215
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:04,940
But now, in Lord Tanjiro Kamado's wake, two Hashira have manifested the mark.

216
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:09,900
Please enlighten us, Lady Kanroji, Lord Tokito.

217
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:16,500
Oh, right! Lady Amane is so gorgeous!

218
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:23,340
Well, you see what happened!

219
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:28,440
My body felt extremely light! Really light! Lighter than usual!

220
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:31,460
Let's see...

221
00:17:31,460 --> 00:17:32,540
Let's see...

222
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:33,460
Um...

223
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:35,780
And then...

224
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:37,460
And then...

225
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:38,960
And then...

226
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:40,860
Bam!

227
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:42,340
Throughout my body!

228
00:17:42,820 --> 00:17:44,100
My limbs went bam!

229
00:17:44,380 --> 00:17:45,840
And my mind went pow!

230
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,720
And I remembered my heart pounding like crazy!

231
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:50,980
And my ears were going ding ding!

232
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:52,640
And ripple ripple!

233
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:53,460
Ripple!

234
00:17:53,460 --> 00:18:07,520
I'm so sorry! Forgive me!

235
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:10,240
I wish I could crawl into a hole right now!

236
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:16,560
Perhaps I can be of help.

237
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:21,820
It's not as if I was aware of the mark manifesting.

238
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:27,740
But when I think about the battle that took place when it did, some things come to mind.

239
00:18:28,580 --> 00:18:31,240
Things that when looking back at it were out of the ordinary.

240
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:36,820
As long as certain conditions are met, I believe that the mark will appear on everyone.

241
00:18:38,120 --> 00:18:40,760
I'll now explain those conditions and how I met them.

242
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:57,820
During the previous battle, I was badly poisoned and left unable to move.

243
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:04,120
I tried to slow down the flow of the poison by using my breathing technique, but before I could,

244
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:11,020
The boy who tried to save me was about to be killed in front of me, which brought back memories of the past.

245
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:15,700
And the overwhelming rage I felt made me lose control of my emotions.

246
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:20,700
I swear at that very moment, my heart rate was over 200.

247
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:25,700
Furthermore, my body felt like it was on fire.

248
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:30,660
As for my temperature, I'm certain it was over 102 degrees.

249
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:34,220
But how could you move in a state like that?

250
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:35,960
Those conditions are fatal.

251
00:19:37,020 --> 00:19:37,860
Yes, that's correct.

252
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:42,100
I think that's the point when those who aren't chosen are killed off.

253
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:50,120
Whether you die or survive in that moment determines whether you get the mark or you become part of the past.

254
00:19:50,120 --> 00:19:56,880
A heart rate over 200 beats a minute.

255
00:19:57,680 --> 00:20:00,640
But your temperature, how do you know it was over 102?

256
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:02,360
Right.

257
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:08,200
Well, you see, I remember when I was being treated at Ms. Kochos, I had an abnormally high fever.

258
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:13,140
In fact, the thermometer reading said 102, like my body heat,

259
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:17,740
when my mark first manifested itself back during my battle with the upper rank.

260
00:20:17,740 --> 00:20:22,200
Is that right?

261
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:26,560
That sounds pretty simple if you ask me.

262
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:30,500
Imagine having such a simple mind that you call this simple.

263
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:31,780
I envy you.

264
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:34,220
What did you just say?

265
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:35,260
Nothing.

266
00:20:35,260 --> 00:20:43,520
So the Hashira's top priority is to awaken these marks, right?

267
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:48,240
If so, you have my word that we'll figure out how.

268
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:52,400
Please let the Master know he may rest easy trusting us to do so.

269
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,720
Thank you for your reassurance.

270
00:20:55,580 --> 00:21:02,060
That said, I must relay just one thing regarding any training for manifesting the mark.

271
00:21:02,060 --> 00:21:03,680
What would that be?

272
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:10,500
I apologize to those whose marks have already appeared, as you have no choice in the matter.

273
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:15,820
All of those who manifest a mark, eventually, without exception.

274
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:38,320
I understand.

275
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:44,440
But if that is the case, then I wonder what will become of me, good lord.

276
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:48,560
If that's everything from Lady Amane, then excuse me.

277
00:21:49,060 --> 00:21:50,020
Not so fast.

278
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:51,780
Nobody here excused you.

279
00:21:52,220 --> 00:21:56,320
We still haven't decided what our respective roles will be in manifesting the mark.

280
00:21:57,040 --> 00:21:59,040
I'll let you six discuss that.

281
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:00,840
It doesn't concern me.

282
00:22:00,840 --> 00:22:04,160
What do you mean it doesn't concern you?

283
00:22:04,720 --> 00:22:07,300
Seems you've forgotten you're also a Hashira.

284
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:12,940
Or you're bluffing, trying to get a head start on training to manifest the mark.

285
00:22:13,300 --> 00:22:14,980
But you're needed here in the meeting.

286
00:22:19,060 --> 00:22:21,060
Hey, you! Get back here!

287
00:22:21,580 --> 00:22:24,460
Mr. Tomioka, I ask you to explain yourself.

288
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:27,400
We cannot dismiss this without reason.

289
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:33,180
It's just I'm not like the rest of you.

290
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:35,500
I'm not satisfied.

291
00:22:36,460 --> 00:22:39,300
You said the same thing before, Tenyou, Tomioka.

292
00:22:39,680 --> 00:22:42,040
You looking down on us right now?

293
00:22:42,620 --> 00:22:44,360
No fighting, okay?

294
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:45,760
Let's calm down.

295
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:49,520
Get back here!

296
00:22:51,140 --> 00:22:52,780
No! No, don't!

297
00:22:52,780 --> 00:22:53,460
Ah!

298
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:55,560
Yeah!

299
00:22:55,560 --> 00:22:55,920
Yeah!

300
00:22:57,400 --> 00:23:02,200
Sit down.

301
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:05,500
Let's continue our discussion.

302
00:23:06,460 --> 00:23:07,860
As I have a proposal.

303
00:23:10,340 --> 00:23:10,900
Here.

304
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:12,160
Wow!

305
00:23:12,420 --> 00:23:13,620
Thank you so much!

306
00:23:14,700 --> 00:23:16,620
Jeez, you sure have an appetite.

307
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:20,920
Hey, where are those three little ones and your kid sister?

308
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:22,800
I haven't seen Aoi, either.

309
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:27,760
Since there aren't any swordsmen in critical condition, they've been outside playing with

310
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:28,220
Nezuko.

311
00:23:29,300 --> 00:23:32,060
It's thanks to that she's starting to speak little by little.

312
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:34,440
Oh, I had no idea.

313
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:35,620
Sounds peaceful.

314
00:23:37,020 --> 00:23:38,700
This rice dumpling is delicious!

315
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:39,860
Yeah, yeah.

316
00:23:40,020 --> 00:23:40,620
I hear you.

317
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:41,020
Okay.

318
00:23:41,820 --> 00:23:46,520
Well, enjoy the peace while you can, because that yellow-haired kid should be back soon.

319
00:23:53,520 --> 00:23:55,180
Oh, Mr. Zenitsu!

320
00:23:55,840 --> 00:23:57,640
Does this mean you're back from your mission?

321
00:23:58,100 --> 00:23:58,820
Hey, Kyo!

322
00:23:59,040 --> 00:23:59,860
Safe and sound!

323
00:23:59,860 --> 00:24:00,740
Everyone!

324
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:03,900
Mr. Zenitsu is back from his mission!

325
00:24:08,420 --> 00:24:11,340
Mr. Zenitsu, thank you for all of your hard work.

326
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:13,440
Thank you for your hard work!

327
00:24:13,820 --> 00:24:16,020
Did you three gather here just for me?

328
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:17,380
That's so nice.

329
00:24:17,440 --> 00:24:18,780
You didn't have to do that.

330
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:21,280
Man, that whole mission, I kept thinking.

331
00:24:21,280 --> 00:24:24,000
I'm gonna die, I'm gonna die, I'm gonna die, I don't wanna die!

332
00:24:24,440 --> 00:24:28,180
But then I thought about how devastated you'd all be if I did die.

333
00:24:28,460 --> 00:24:29,460
So I did it!

334
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:31,980
You'd be sad if I weren't around, right?

335
00:24:32,260 --> 00:24:33,720
Sorry, not really, no!

336
00:24:33,860 --> 00:24:38,480
But still, we're always glad to see you come back in one piece!

337
00:24:39,380 --> 00:24:40,360
Oh, thanks.

338
00:24:45,320 --> 00:24:48,580
Oh, Mr. Zenitsu, I'm glad to see you're finally back.

339
00:24:49,020 --> 00:24:50,260
Thank you for your hard work.

340
00:24:50,260 --> 00:24:54,920
Miss Howie, you missed me while I was on that mission, didn't you?

341
00:24:55,100 --> 00:24:56,720
You did miss me, right?

342
00:24:57,620 --> 00:24:59,680
I don't know if I'd put it like that.

343
00:25:09,620 --> 00:25:11,400
Welcome home.

344
00:25:11,400 --> 00:25:22,780
You're so cute, I'm gonna die!

345
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:24,260
Then go right ahead.

346
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:26,740
Hey, am I going crazy?

347
00:25:27,080 --> 00:25:28,120
Or did you just talk?

348
00:25:28,240 --> 00:25:28,700
For me?

349
00:25:29,020 --> 00:25:29,600
Just for me?

350
00:25:29,820 --> 00:25:30,880
You learn to talk for me?

351
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:31,980
That makes me so happy!

352
00:25:31,980 --> 00:25:34,780
Oh, please go somewhere else.

353
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:36,440
Does this mean you and I are getting married?

354
00:25:37,700 --> 00:25:39,520
Get away from her, Greek!

355
00:25:39,700 --> 00:25:44,080
You are a lovely sight to see in the moonlight, but in the sunlight, you're even more beautiful!

356
00:25:44,620 --> 00:25:45,380
Megafizant!

357
00:25:45,620 --> 00:25:50,240
After we get married, I'll make sure you have sushi and eel every day of our married life!

358
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:53,860
Welcome home, Inosuke!

359
00:25:57,860 --> 00:25:58,860
In...

360
00:25:58,860 --> 00:26:00,300
Inosuke?

361
00:26:00,980 --> 00:26:03,340
Inosuke, welcome home!

362
00:26:03,340 --> 00:26:07,340
Where the hell is that guy?

363
00:26:07,600 --> 00:26:09,340
I think I'll go kill him!

364
00:26:09,460 --> 00:26:10,860
Hey, stop talking like that!

365
00:26:11,640 --> 00:26:14,300
Come to think of it, where's that boarhead kid?

366
00:26:14,960 --> 00:26:15,880
You mean Inosuke?

367
00:26:16,500 --> 00:26:18,340
Huh, he was here this morning.

368
00:26:19,320 --> 00:26:23,000
Your kid's sister sure has been getting schooled by that boarhead, you know?

369
00:26:23,740 --> 00:26:24,680
What's that mean?

370
00:26:25,020 --> 00:26:26,300
Let's check, shall we?

371
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:27,440
Inosuke!

372
00:26:27,580 --> 00:26:28,120
Inosuke!

373
00:26:28,260 --> 00:26:28,780
Inosuke!

374
00:26:28,940 --> 00:26:29,520
Inosuke!

375
00:26:30,020 --> 00:26:30,660
Inosuke!

376
00:26:30,940 --> 00:26:31,620
Inosuke!

377
00:26:31,760 --> 00:26:32,760
Big Boss Inosuke!

378
00:26:32,760 --> 00:26:34,300
Big Boss Inosuke!

379
00:26:34,480 --> 00:26:35,000
Inosuke!

380
00:26:35,100 --> 00:26:35,540
Inosuke!

381
00:26:35,640 --> 00:26:36,100
Inosuke!

382
00:26:36,180 --> 00:26:36,640
Inosuke!

383
00:26:36,640 --> 00:26:36,840
Inosuke!

384
00:26:37,060 --> 00:26:39,880
He's been dead set on making sure she learns his name.

385
00:26:40,560 --> 00:26:41,040
Really?

386
00:26:41,320 --> 00:26:42,760
That's funny, I had no idea.

387
00:26:43,440 --> 00:26:46,020
By the way, do you have any more of these rice dumplings?

388
00:26:46,680 --> 00:26:47,940
You're not done eating?

389
00:26:57,940 --> 00:27:00,080
Hey, Mr. Hageneska!

390
00:27:00,080 --> 00:27:03,400
Have your wounds healed yet?

391
00:27:04,960 --> 00:27:05,860
Oh, good.

392
00:27:09,460 --> 00:27:10,020
Um...

393
00:27:10,020 --> 00:27:13,660
Are you sure you're feeling all right?

394
00:27:13,660 --> 00:27:17,220
Oh, my sword.

395
00:27:17,220 --> 00:27:19,400
Oh, thank you very much.

396
00:27:22,180 --> 00:27:24,080
Mr. Rengoku's sword guard!

397
00:27:25,660 --> 00:27:27,360
Thanks for protecting Kotetsu.

398
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:29,140
I owe it all to you.

399
00:27:29,140 --> 00:27:32,400
Why don't you come take a seat?

400
00:27:32,800 --> 00:27:33,660
Are you all right?

401
00:27:41,660 --> 00:27:42,720
My blade?

402
00:27:43,060 --> 00:27:44,240
Okay, I'll look at it.

403
00:27:44,240 --> 00:27:58,960
Wow, it's an even deeper shade of black.

404
00:27:58,960 --> 00:28:02,060
That's some high-quality steel there.

405
00:28:02,500 --> 00:28:05,560
So the swordsmen who wielded it must have been exceptionally strong.

406
00:28:07,340 --> 00:28:09,300
The character for destroy.

407
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:12,700
The swordsmith who first forged this,

408
00:28:13,180 --> 00:28:16,280
meant for it to destroy all demons it came into contact with.

409
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:18,660
He didn't even engrave his name.

410
00:28:18,660 --> 00:28:21,240
All he left behind was this one character.

411
00:28:22,380 --> 00:28:25,880
I'm told the hierarchy system started after this sword was forged.

412
00:28:26,320 --> 00:28:28,020
And only the Hashira had the words

413
00:28:28,020 --> 00:28:30,540
destroyer of demons engraved on their swords.

414
00:28:31,080 --> 00:28:32,220
I had no idea.

415
00:28:32,540 --> 00:28:33,360
That's incredible.

416
00:28:34,240 --> 00:28:36,940
But I don't remember seeing this character

417
00:28:36,940 --> 00:28:38,840
during my previous battle.

418
00:28:39,700 --> 00:28:40,020
Huh?

419
00:28:40,020 --> 00:28:42,480
I told you.

420
00:28:42,860 --> 00:28:45,420
That's because I only finished the first stage of honing

421
00:28:45,420 --> 00:28:48,620
before you brats took it away and used it against my will.

422
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:51,180
I hadn't even finished removing the rust yet.

423
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:52,860
I ought to kill you.

424
00:28:53,360 --> 00:28:54,000
I'm sorry.

425
00:28:54,580 --> 00:28:56,260
My wounds still haven't fully healed.

426
00:28:56,480 --> 00:28:58,620
I can't stop the tears from flowing out.

427
00:28:58,920 --> 00:29:00,920
It hurts so bad I can't take it anymore.

428
00:29:01,380 --> 00:29:03,620
Thanks to the interruptions from that demon in you brats,

429
00:29:03,620 --> 00:29:05,700
I have to start honing it again from scratch.

430
00:29:06,120 --> 00:29:06,940
From scratch!

431
00:29:06,940 --> 00:29:10,660
In terms of severity, the kid's injuries are as bad as yours.

432
00:29:11,040 --> 00:29:13,840
The bones in his body got totally pulverized.

433
00:29:18,600 --> 00:29:20,260
I'm gonna kill you!

434
00:29:20,560 --> 00:29:21,820
Did you hear what I said?

435
00:29:22,220 --> 00:29:23,500
Listen to me, Tanjiro.

436
00:29:23,960 --> 00:29:26,820
You're gonna bring me rice dumplings until the day you die!

437
00:29:27,020 --> 00:29:27,900
You got that?

438
00:29:28,140 --> 00:29:29,000
Rice dumplings!

439
00:29:29,740 --> 00:29:30,100
Yes!

440
00:29:30,100 --> 00:29:31,520
I'll bring them every day!

441
00:29:32,320 --> 00:29:33,860
Thank you for your hard work.

442
00:29:34,220 --> 00:29:34,960
Dead well.

443
00:29:34,960 --> 00:29:37,820
I've heard the rumors about him,

444
00:29:38,080 --> 00:29:39,820
but he sure is a piece of work.

445
00:29:40,980 --> 00:29:43,300
That was actually a mild outburst.

446
00:29:43,840 --> 00:29:45,140
He must be in a lot of pain.

447
00:29:45,740 --> 00:29:46,220
Seriously?

448
00:29:46,740 --> 00:29:48,980
Can you be any noisier over there?

449
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:49,560
Oh.

450
00:29:50,220 --> 00:29:51,280
Hey there, Genya.

451
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:53,000
We're done now.

452
00:29:53,680 --> 00:29:54,520
Sorry for that.

453
00:29:54,680 --> 00:29:54,960
He's just...

454
00:29:54,960 --> 00:30:05,180
No, Skate!

455
00:30:05,340 --> 00:30:07,140
You can't just break windows like that!

456
00:30:08,800 --> 00:30:10,080
Are you an idiot?

457
00:30:10,500 --> 00:30:12,220
Lady Kojo's gonna kill you!

458
00:30:14,140 --> 00:30:14,740
Quiet!

459
00:30:14,740 --> 00:30:15,360
He he he!

460
00:30:15,640 --> 00:30:16,620
Coming through!

461
00:30:17,180 --> 00:30:20,780
I wish they just put me in another room.

462
00:30:20,780 --> 00:30:23,060
Training, training, training!

463
00:30:23,720 --> 00:30:26,100
Group strength training is about to start!

464
00:30:26,920 --> 00:30:28,140
Group strength training?

465
00:30:28,560 --> 00:30:31,420
The strongest will gather and train their hardest.

466
00:30:32,180 --> 00:30:33,840
Blah blah blah, something mark!

467
00:30:34,220 --> 00:30:34,640
Huh?

468
00:30:34,780 --> 00:30:35,720
What is that about?

469
00:30:36,320 --> 00:30:37,840
I have no idea!

470
00:30:38,360 --> 00:30:38,900
I see.

471
00:30:38,900 --> 00:30:46,580
As for the Hashira training for the Demon Slayer Corps,

472
00:30:47,200 --> 00:30:50,300
I think we've settled on most of the finer details of our strategy.

473
00:30:51,660 --> 00:30:52,140
Okay.

474
00:30:52,520 --> 00:30:54,320
What about the duration and start date?

475
00:30:55,340 --> 00:30:57,620
I propose we begin in three days' time.

476
00:30:58,080 --> 00:30:59,080
Can we really do that?

477
00:30:59,200 --> 00:30:59,920
It's so soon.

478
00:31:00,780 --> 00:31:02,880
We're racing against time as it is.

479
00:31:03,580 --> 00:31:07,760
And since we have no way of knowing how Muzan Kibutsuji will make his first move,

480
00:31:07,760 --> 00:31:10,800
I'd like for us to be prepared as much as possible.

481
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:12,540
I agree.

482
00:31:13,200 --> 00:31:15,260
If the demons run rampant again,

483
00:31:15,920 --> 00:31:18,820
it'll be too much for us Hashira alone to handle.

484
00:31:20,080 --> 00:31:21,920
But if we're busy with training,

485
00:31:22,500 --> 00:31:24,220
won't that leave us open to an attack?

486
00:31:25,460 --> 00:31:26,120
Not quite.

487
00:31:26,620 --> 00:31:30,820
As we can assume the demon's top priority right now is capturing Nezuko Kamado.

488
00:31:31,460 --> 00:31:34,360
And ever since the recent attack on the Swordsmith Village,

489
00:31:35,140 --> 00:31:37,500
demon sightings have been dwindling considerably.

490
00:31:38,460 --> 00:31:39,580
If that's the case,

491
00:31:40,460 --> 00:31:45,620
up until now we Hashira have been too busy dealing with demons to train anyone except our own Suguko.

492
00:31:46,620 --> 00:31:47,960
Even if for a short time,

493
00:31:48,040 --> 00:31:51,980
this would be our only chance to provide mentorship to the entire Demon Slayer Corps.

494
00:31:53,540 --> 00:31:55,920
This training is of the utmost importance.

495
00:31:55,920 --> 00:31:57,820
Therefore,

496
00:31:58,620 --> 00:32:00,460
it's vital that we don't waste time.

497
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:01,620
I propose,

498
00:32:01,980 --> 00:32:04,120
we begin Hashira training in three days.

499
00:32:05,080 --> 00:32:06,000
Save your breath,

500
00:32:06,100 --> 00:32:06,820
Mr. Himejima.

501
00:32:07,260 --> 00:32:09,200
I was sold the moment you started talking.

502
00:32:10,200 --> 00:32:11,480
I too am in agreement.

503
00:32:11,480 --> 00:32:13,780
I have no objections.

504
00:32:15,640 --> 00:32:16,200
Agreed.

505
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:18,340
Three days is plenty.

506
00:32:20,120 --> 00:32:23,920
Are we certain the training can be handled by just as active Hashira?

507
00:32:23,920 --> 00:32:28,640
I was considering asking the retired Hashira to lend a hand as well.

508
00:32:29,140 --> 00:32:30,520
Are there any objections?

509
00:32:31,140 --> 00:32:32,680
That sounds good to me.

510
00:32:33,620 --> 00:32:34,760
With that decided,

511
00:32:35,300 --> 00:32:37,880
all that's left is Mr. Tomioka.

512
00:32:37,880 --> 00:32:46,220
I finally managed to get back from my mission,

513
00:32:46,540 --> 00:32:47,760
and now we have to train.

514
00:32:48,140 --> 00:32:49,040
Just kill me.

515
00:32:49,620 --> 00:32:50,660
Are you heading there now,

516
00:32:50,760 --> 00:32:51,240
Zenni too?

517
00:32:51,960 --> 00:32:52,480
Unfortunately.

518
00:32:52,960 --> 00:32:56,200
And I heard that we have to train under every Hashira one by one.

519
00:32:56,620 --> 00:32:56,980
What?

520
00:32:57,120 --> 00:32:57,500
Really?

521
00:32:57,800 --> 00:32:58,640
That's great.

522
00:32:59,420 --> 00:33:01,580
There's nothing great about what I just said.

523
00:33:01,640 --> 00:33:02,840
It's awful and hellish.

524
00:33:03,240 --> 00:33:04,600
Whoever thought up this torture,

525
00:33:04,960 --> 00:33:05,600
kill yourself.

526
00:33:05,880 --> 00:33:06,180
Hey,

527
00:33:06,180 --> 00:33:09,440
getting to train with someone who's ranked above you is a privilege,

528
00:33:09,800 --> 00:33:11,500
and a shortcut to getting stronger.

529
